__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
# harness runtime state (project-local, under .opencode/harness/): ignore the
# DIRECTORY, not a hand-listed set of files. A per-file list only ever covers
# what someone remembered to add, which is how ui-state.json leaked; the
# wildcard makes a new state file ignored by default. `skills/` stays trackable
# because harness only ever READS it. `.opencode/harness.jsonc` is per-project
# CONFIG and sits one level up, so it is deliberately NOT ignored.
.opencode/harness/*
!.opencode/harness/skills/
# atomic-write temp files: ui-state.json.tmp, harness.jsonc.tmp
.opencode/**/*.tmp
.venv/
/build/
# stray chat exports, MBs of them at the repo root
freebuff-chat-*.md
# anchored: a bare `build/` also ignored harness/data/skills/build/, which
# silently kept a new skill out of every commit (the two files already there
# were tracked before the rule existed)
